# - Wikipedia, Bouyon music (opened): "Prominent bouyon groups include Windward Caribbean Kulture (WCK); Roots, Stems and Branches (RSB); and First Serenade", citing Shepherd and Laing, Continuum Encyclopedia of Popular Music of the World (2005), p. 43.
# - Academia.edu, Dominica chapter (Continuum text, search result and opened excerpts): "Among the leading bouyon bands are WCK, RSB (Roots, Stems and Branches) and First Serenade (an older band that spans almost the entire history of popular music in Dominica)"; discography entry "First Serenade. Chant Dem. First Serenade. 1997: Dominica"; late 1990s Dominican bouyon influence on Barbadian ring bang (Square One, Krosfyah) and Trinidad soca.
# - Music of Dominica, 2007 Schools Wikipedia selection via EPFL dlab (opened): 1980s soca "producing bands like RSB, Windward Caribbean Kulture (WCK) and First Serenade"; WCK formed in 1988 fusing cadence-lypso with jing ping, the result became bouyon.
# - GuideDM, Voices of Dominica (opened): WCK created bouyon with "Conch Shell" and "Balance Batty"; "Serenade Band (First Serenade) and Effects Band helped refine and reimagine the bouyon sound"; World Creole Music Festival since 1997.
# - Mondo Local, WCMF 2018 field report (opened): "Dominican legendary band First Serenade", blend of Cadence Lypso, Bouyon, Soca and Zouk; formed over 34 years ago (report on the 2018 edition); lifetime achievement award during the 1999 World Creole Music Festival; over 20 albums to date including a recent 2018 single; 2018 Friday set described in detail: horn trio of trumpet, trombone and saxophone, bass, drums and guitars, two lead singers, one extended medley running cadence lypso, bouyon, zouk and calypso, closing Carnival medley.
# - AFP via ArtDaily, WCMF 2018 (opened): First Serenade, an 11 piece Dominican band that started off playing in a church in the 1980s, reunited for the festival after losing their instruments in the hurricane (Maria, September 2017); trombonist Christopher Dangleben quoted on the fusion and on lyrics that promote peace, humanity and the island; First Serenade plays bouyon, a blend of jing ping with bele, reggae and soca; Derek Peters credited in the article with creating the style.
# - Riches Karayib, WCMF 2022 (opened): lineup included "the almost 40 year old band First Serenade" alongside WCK, TK International, Midnight Groovers and Signal Band.
# - Writeups24, WCMF 2025 schedule (search result): Night 2, Saturday October 25, 2025, lists First Serenade alongside Vybz Kartel, Spice, Asa Bantan, WCK and the Bouyon Assembly; the 2026 Creole season calendar lists First Serenade Band among the participants of the Belles Combo Benefit Concert on October 3, 2026.
# - Dominica Weekly, Ti Vilaj Kweyol Day 2, Tuesday 20 October 2026 (opened): First Serenade billed at 4:20 PM as "Bouyon legends", "one of Dominica's most beloved Bouyon bands", at the Botanic Gardens, Roseau.
# - Dominica Weekly, Creole in the Park 2008 (search result): First Serenade band performing hit tracks from the past on day one, WCK closing the same day.
# - YouTube, First Serenade Band Official channel (opened): bio begins "The First Serenade Band, with years in the music arena, emerges from the picturesque village of Point Michel nestled on Dominica's south western coast"; channel video list includes Calypso Old Mass Medley, First Serenade Band Ft. Halibut "Riches of Dominica", Bef La, One Two Three (Under De Mango Tree), Do Di Wiper, Rough Up De Session, Enjoy Your Life (Official Music Video), Indian Tramp, Charle L'amour, Donkey Tricks 96, De Whinery 96, Easy Feeling, Take Yuh Foot, Real Mas (Bouyon 2026), Ti Vilaj Kweyol Live 2025, Millennium Train live at WCMF 2025, O La E Ye live at WCMF 2025, Bouyon Rhythm (Bouyon 2025), Dancing Time with Rangerman (Bouyon 2025), Lavi Lanmou Nou Vle, Still Blazin Medley featuring Nayee, Pa Goumen 97, Chicken Rhythm. The 14 CD albums figure and the style list (zouk, reggae, bouyon, soca, salsa, calypso, soukous) come from the channel description as quoted by Feedspot (search result); the album count is attributed to the band's own presentation in the profile text.
# - YouTube, "First Serenade Band - Take Yuh Foot" official video (opened): written by Lloyd "Lloydie" Jno Baptiste; performed by The First Serenade Band; produced by Logically Don Productions and Maskman; arranged by Donavan Gabriel; mixed and mastered at Logically Don Productions; vocals recorded at Dernel Green (DernzMuzsik, spelling as published); riddim production Arade "Maskman" Moses; cover art KimmieDesignz; copyright 2026 First Serenade Band; description calls Lloydie the lead singer of the band and the track a bouyon riddim record; follow links list Instagram, Facebook and SoundCloud as /firstserenadeband and YouTube as @firstserenadebandofficial.
